cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "HighRes-EERIE-NorthAtlantic-Evaluation: winter extremes, the NAO and high-resolution climate models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pradhan"
    given-names: "Himansu Kesari"
date-released: 2026-11-05
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TunaHim/HighRes-EERIE-NorthAtlantic-Evaluation"
url: "https://tunahim.github.io/HighRes-EERIE-NorthAtlantic-Evaluation/"
abstract: >-
  An exploratory evaluation of public output from the EU project EERIE (ICON-ESM-ER and
  IFS-FESOM2-SR) against ERA5 and E-OBS: the winter North Atlantic Oscillation, precipitation
  and temperature extremes over the UK and Ireland, the link between them, the weather behind
  the heaviest rain days, and how the conclusions depend on resolution (9 km versus 28 km) and
  on internal variability.
keywords:
  - climate model evaluation
  - North Atlantic Oscillation
  - precipitation extremes
  - high-resolution climate models
  - EERIE
  - ERA5
  - E-OBS
  - United Kingdom
  - Ireland
